/* Verse Games: THE WHOLE COUNSEL · Ezekiel chapters 6-10
   Verse text is filled/verified from the KJV by tools/fill-verses.js */
VG.registerBibleChapters("ezekiel", [
{n:6, name:"Against the Mountains of Israel", seal:{ref:"Ezekiel 6:8",verse:"Yet will I leave a remnant, that ye may have some that shall escape the sword among the nations, when ye shall be scattered through the countries."}, facts:["Did you know the phrase 'they shall know that I am the LORD' rings through chapter 6 four times, at verses 7, 10, 13, and 14, like a drumbeat under the judgment?","Did you know God told Ezekiel to prophesy against the mountains themselves, because Israel had turned every high hill and green tree into a shrine, offering sweet savour to idols under every thick oak (Ezekiel 6:13)?","Did you know that even in this dark chapter God promises a remnant, some who would escape the sword among the nations and remember Him there (Ezekiel 6:8-9)?"], questions:[
{q:"What did God command Ezekiel to do?", options:["Set thy face toward the mountains of Israel, and prophesy against them","Turn thy face toward the sea, and prophesy to the waves","Go down to Jerusalem, and comfort the elders","Flee to the wilderness, and hide thy face"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 6:2",verse:"Son of man, set thy face toward the mountains of Israel, and prophesy against them,", insight:"God's call is not always comfort; sometimes the prophet must face the hard word and speak it plainly."},
{q:"Whom did the Lord address in His message?", options:["The mountains, and the hills, the rivers, and the valleys","The kings, and the princes of Judah","The priests, and the Levites of the temple","The elders, and the scribes of Jerusalem"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 6:3",verse:"And say, Ye mountains of Israel, hear the word of the Lord GOD; Thus saith the Lord GOD to the mountains, and to the hills, to the rivers, and to the valleys; Behold, I, even I, will bring a sword upon you, and I will destroy your high places.", insight:"When the land itself is addressed, the whole nation is on trial; creation hears what men refuse to hear."},
{q:"What would God bring upon the mountains?", options:["A sword, and the destruction of their high places","A flood, and the washing of the valleys","A famine, and the drying of the rivers","A fire, and the melting of the hills"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 6:3",verse:"And say, Ye mountains of Israel, hear the word of the Lord GOD; Thus saith the Lord GOD to the mountains, and to the hills, to the rivers, and to the valleys; Behold, I, even I, will bring a sword upon you, and I will destroy your high places.", insight:"The high places men built to other gods would be the first to fall; what competes with God cannot stand."},
{q:"What would become of their altars and images?", options:["The altars desolate, and the images broken","The altars gilded, and the images polished","The altars moved, and the images hidden","The altars cleansed, and the images spared"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 6:4",verse:"And your altars shall be desolate, and your images shall be broken: and I will cast down your slain men before your idols.", insight:"God does not reform idols; He breaks them. The only cure for false worship is its end."},
{q:"What would God cast down before their idols?", options:["Their slain men","Their gold and silver","Their broken altars","Their burnt offerings"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 6:4",verse:"And your altars shall be desolate, and your images shall be broken: and I will cast down your slain men before your idols.", insight:"They trusted idols to save them; instead the dead would fall at the idols' feet. Trust what cannot save, and it will watch you fall."},
{q:"Where would God scatter their bones?", options:["Round about their altars","In the wilderness of Sinai","Along the banks of the Jordan","Under the walls of Jerusalem"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 6:5",verse:"And I will lay the dead carcases of the children of Israel before their idols; and I will scatter your bones round about your altars.", insight:"The altars they loved became the graveyards they deserved; sin always buries you where you worshipped it."},
{q:"What would happen in all their dwelling places?", options:["The cities laid waste, and the high places desolate","The cities enlarged, and the high places raised","The cities fortified, and the high places guarded","The cities prospering, and the high places thronged"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 6:6",verse:"In all your dwellingplaces the cities shall be laid waste, and the high places shall be desolate; that your altars may be laid waste and made desolate, and your idols may be broken and cease, and your images may be cut down, and your works may be abolished.", insight:"Judgment touches home and hill alike; no corner of a disobedient life escapes God's hand."},
{q:"What would be cut down and abolished?", options:["Their images, and their works","Their walls, and their towers","Their vineyards, and their fields","Their ships, and their markets"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 6:6",verse:"In all your dwellingplaces the cities shall be laid waste, and the high places shall be desolate; that your altars may be laid waste and made desolate, and your idols may be broken and cease, and your images may be cut down, and your works may be abolished.", insight:"The works of men's hands cannot outlast the word of God's mouth."},
{q:"What would they know when the slain fall in their midst?", options:["That I am the LORD","That the sword is sharp","That the nations are strong","That the idols are silent"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 6:7",verse:"And the slain shall fall in the midst of you, and ye shall know that I am the LORD.", insight:"This is the refrain of Ezekiel: judgment has a purpose, that men may know the LORD."},
{q:"What would God leave?", options:["A remnant that escape the sword among the nations","A city that escapes the famine","A temple that escapes the fire","An army that escapes the battle"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 6:8",verse:"Yet will I leave a remnant, that ye may have some that shall escape the sword among the nations, when ye shall be scattered through the countries.", insight:"Even in wrath, God keeps a remnant; His judgments never cancel His promises."},
{q:"What would the escaped ones do among the nations?", options:["Remember me","Forget their homeland","Serve other gods","Build new altars"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 6:9",verse:"And they that escape of you shall remember me among the nations whither they shall be carried captives, because I am broken with their whorish heart, which hath departed from me, and with their eyes, which go a whoring after their idols: and they shall lothe themselves for the evils which they have committed in all their abominations.", insight:"Exile became a school of remembrance; sometimes we must lose everything to remember God."},
{q:"With what was God broken?", options:["With their whorish heart, which had departed from Him","With their weary feet, which had wandered far","With their empty hands, which had nothing to give","With their silent lips, which would not pray"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 6:9",verse:"And they that escape of you shall remember me among the nations whither they shall be carried captives, because I am broken with their whorish heart, which hath departed from me, and with their eyes, which go a whoring after their idols: and they shall lothe themselves for the evils which they have committed in all their abominations.", insight:"Idolatry is spoken of as unfaithfulness because God takes love personally; He is broken when His people stray."},
{q:"What would they know about God's threatened judgment?", options:["That He had not said it in vain","That He had forgotten it","That He had spoken it in anger only","That He had meant another nation"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 6:10",verse:"And they shall know that I am the LORD, and that I have not said in vain that I would do this evil unto them.", insight:"God's warnings are never empty threats; every word He speaks will prove true."},
{q:"What sign was Ezekiel told to perform?", options:["Smite with thine hand, and stamp with thy foot","Lift up thine hands, and shout aloud","Cover thy head, and sit in silence","Tear thy clothes, and weep bitterly"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 6:11",verse:"Thus saith the Lord GOD; Smite with thine hand, and stamp with thy foot, and say, Alas for all the evil abominations of the house of Israel! for they shall fall by the sword, by the famine, and by the pestilence.", insight:"The prophet's body preaches too; grief and warning can be acted as well as spoken."},
{q:"By what three means would Israel fall?", options:["By the sword, by the famine, and by the pestilence","By the flood, by the fire, and by the hail","By the sword, by the earthquake, and by the storm","By the famine, by the drought, and by the locusts"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 6:11",verse:"Thus saith the Lord GOD; Smite with thine hand, and stamp with thy foot, and say, Alas for all the evil abominations of the house of Israel! for they shall fall by the sword, by the famine, and by the pestilence.", insight:"No escape route is left unguarded; the only safety is repentance, not distance."},
{q:"What would become of him that is far off?", options:["He shall die of the pestilence","He shall escape to Egypt","He shall hide in the caves","He shall return in peace"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 6:12",verse:"He that is far off shall die of the pestilence; and he that is near shall fall by the sword; and he that remaineth and is besieged shall die by the famine: thus will I accomplish my fury upon them.", insight:"Distance does not deliver; you cannot outrun the judgment of God."},
{q:"What would become of him that is near?", options:["He shall fall by the sword","He shall be taken as a slave","He shall be sold for silver","He shall be crowned king"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 6:12",verse:"He that is far off shall die of the pestilence; and he that is near shall fall by the sword; and he that remaineth and is besieged shall die by the famine: thus will I accomplish my fury upon them.", insight:"Near or far, no place is safe when God's fury is accomplished; the land itself becomes the courtroom."},
{q:"When would they know that He is the LORD?", options:["When their slain men lie among their idols round about their altars","When the sun rises over the mountains","When the harvest fills the barns","When the priests blow the trumpets"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 6:13",verse:"Then shall ye know that I am the LORD, when their slain men shall be among their idols round about their altars, upon every high hill, in all the tops of the mountains, and under every green tree, and under every thick oak, the place where they did offer sweet savour to all their idols.", insight:"They would learn God's name at last, but among the ruins of the idols they loved; knowing Him late is better than never."},
{q:"In what places had they offered sweet savour to their idols?", options:["Upon every high hill, on the mountain tops, under every green tree, and under every thick oak","In the courts of the temple alone","At the gates of Jerusalem only","In the wilderness of Sinai"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 6:13",verse:"Then shall ye know that I am the LORD, when their slain men shall be among their idols round about their altars, upon every high hill, in all the tops of the mountains, and under every green tree, and under every thick oak, the place where they did offer sweet savour to all their idols.", insight:"Every beautiful place had been made ugly with idolatry; God notices what we do with His gifts."},
{q:"How desolate would God make the land?", options:["More desolate than the wilderness toward Diblath","As a fruitful field","As a garden of spices","As a land of milk and honey"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 6:14",verse:"So will I stretch out my hand upon them, and make the land desolate, yea, more desolate than the wilderness toward Diblath, in all their habitations: and they shall know that I am the LORD.", insight:"The land of promise could become a wilderness of judgment; blessing forfeited becomes desolation."}
]},
{n:7, name:"The End Is Come", seal:{ref:"Ezekiel 7:9",verse:"And mine eye shall not spare, neither will I have pity: I will recompense thee according to thy ways and thine abominations that are in the midst of thee; and ye shall know that I am the LORD that smiteth."}, facts:["Did you know chapter 7 opens with one of the starkest lines in the prophets: 'An end, the end is come upon the four corners of the land' (Ezekiel 7:2)?","Did you know that in the day of wrath their silver and gold would not deliver them, because their wealth had become the stumblingblock of their iniquity (Ezekiel 7:19)?","Did you know the chapter ends with the king mourning and the prince clothed with desolation, for God would do to them according to their deserts (Ezekiel 7:27)?"], questions:[
{q:"Upon how many corners of the land is the end come?", options:["The four corners","The two borders","The seven hills","The twelve gates"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 7:2",verse:"Also, thou son of man, thus saith the Lord GOD unto the land of Israel; An end, the end is come upon the four corners of the land.", insight:"Four corners means every direction; no one is outside the reach of this word."},
{q:"How would God judge Israel?", options:["According to thy ways, and recompense all thine abominations","According to thy riches, and recompense all thy gains","According to thy strength, and recompense all thy battles","According to thy priests, and recompense all thy sacrifices"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 7:3",verse:"Now is the end come upon thee, and I will send mine anger upon thee, and will judge thee according to thy ways, and will recompense upon thee all thine abominations.", insight:"God's judgment fits the life lived; He recompenses according to ways, not wishes."},
{q:"Would God's eye spare?", options:["Mine eye shall not spare, neither will I have pity","His eye would spare the righteous","His eye would pity the young","His eye would overlook the small sins"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 7:4",verse:"And mine eye shall not spare thee, neither will I have pity: but I will recompense thy ways upon thee, and thine abominations shall be in the midst of thee: and ye shall know that I am the LORD.", insight:"A day comes when mercy has been refused so long that pity gives way to justice; do not presume on delay."},
{q:"What kind of evil is coming?", options:["An evil, an only evil","A small trouble, soon past","A common trial, often seen","A distant rumor, soon forgotten"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 7:5",verse:"Thus saith the Lord GOD; An evil, an only evil, behold, is come.", insight:"An only evil: a judgment without precedent, and hopefully without repeat; take it seriously the first time."},
{q:"What does the end do?", options:["It watcheth for thee","It sleepeth in the night","It wandereth far away","It hideth in the hills"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 7:6",verse:"An end is come, the end is come: it watcheth for thee; behold, it is come.", insight:"The end is pictured as awake and watching; judgment is not asleep, even when sinners are."},
{q:"What is the coming day called?", options:["The day of trouble","The day of feasting","The day of harvest","The day of rest"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 7:7",verse:"The morning is come unto thee, O thou that dwellest in the land: the time is come, the day of trouble is near, and not the sounding again of the mountains.", insight:"The morning they waited for would dawn as trouble; longed-for days can become dreaded ones."},
{q:"By what name would they know God in that day?", options:["The LORD that smiteth","The LORD that blesseth","The LORD that hideth","The LORD that waiteth"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 7:9",verse:"And mine eye shall not spare, neither will I have pity: I will recompense thee according to thy ways and thine abominations that are in the midst of thee; and ye shall know that I am the LORD that smiteth.", insight:"They had refused to know Him as the LORD who saves; they would know Him as the LORD who smites."},
{q:"The rod hath blossomed; what had budded?", options:["Pride","Humility","Wisdom","Mercy"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 7:10",verse:"Behold the day, behold, it is come: the morning is gone forth; the rod hath blossomed, pride hath budded.", insight:"Pride buds before it blooms into ruin; cut it early, while it is only a bud."},
{q:"Into what is violence risen up?", options:["Into a rod of wickedness","Into a crown of glory","Into a shield of strength","Into a song of triumph"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 7:11",verse:"Violence is risen up into a rod of wickedness: none of them shall remain, nor of their multitude, nor of any of theirs: neither shall there be wailing for them.", insight:"Violence grows into a rod that beats its own maker; the wicked forge the instrument of their fall."},
{q:"How many of them shall remain?", options:["None of them shall remain","A tenth shall remain","The strong shall remain","The rich shall remain"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 7:11",verse:"Violence is risen up into a rod of wickedness: none of them shall remain, nor of their multitude, nor of any of theirs: neither shall there be wailing for them.", insight:"None shall remain: when God empties the house of pride, nothing of it is kept."},
{q:"Why should the buyer not rejoice, nor the seller mourn?", options:["For wrath is upon all the multitude","For peace is upon all the land","For plenty is upon all the houses","For joy is upon all the people"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 7:12",verse:"The time is come, the day draweth near: let not the buyer rejoice, nor the seller mourn: for wrath is upon all the multitude thereof.", insight:"Wrath levels every market; in the day of judgment, buyer and seller share one fate."},
{q:"What shall the seller not return to?", options:["That which is sold","His former house","His native land","His family table"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 7:13",verse:"For the seller shall not return to that which is sold, although they were yet alive: for the vision is touching the whole multitude thereof, which shall not return; neither shall any strengthen himself in the iniquity of his life.", insight:"The sale is final and the loss is lasting; some bargains can never be undone."},
{q:"Why does none go to the battle though the trumpet is blown?", options:["For God's wrath is upon all the multitude","For the army is well prepared","For the enemy has fled","For the king has made peace"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 7:14",verse:"They have blown the trumpet, even to make all ready; but none goeth to the battle: for my wrath is upon all the multitude thereof.", insight:"They prepared for a battle God had already decided; no trumpet can rally men under wrath."},
{q:"What is without, and what within?", options:["The sword without, and the pestilence and the famine within","The rain without, and the drought within","The enemy without, and the friend within","The night without, and the day within"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 7:15",verse:"The sword is without, and the pestilence and the famine within: he that is in the field shall die with the sword; and he that is in the city, famine and pestilence shall devour him.", insight:"No direction is safe: danger outside the walls, death inside them; only God is a refuge."},
{q:"Like what will the escaped ones mourn on the mountains?", options:["Like doves of the valleys","Like lions of the desert","Like eagles of the rocks","Like ravens of the field"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 7:16",verse:"But they that escape of them shall escape, and shall be on the mountains like doves of the valleys, all of them mourning, every one for his iniquity.", insight:"The proud become like doves, soft and mourning; judgment humbles every heart, and mourning for iniquity is its first wisdom."},
{q:"What shall knees be weak as?", options:["As water","As iron","As stone","As brass"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 7:17",verse:"All hands shall be feeble, and all knees shall be weak as water.", insight:"All strength melts in the day of wrath; human knees were never meant to stand alone."},
{q:"Where shall they cast their silver?", options:["In the streets","In the temple","In the river","In the tombs"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 7:19",verse:"They shall cast their silver in the streets, and their gold shall be removed: their silver and their gold shall not be able to deliver them in the day of the wrath of the LORD: they shall not satisfy their souls, neither fill their bowels: because it is the stumblingblock of their iniquity.", insight:"The silver they trusted becomes street litter; what you worship today, you may throw away tomorrow."},
{q:"Why was Ezekiel told, 'Make a chain'?", options:["For the land is full of bloody crimes, and the city is full of violence","For the temple is full of singers, and the courts full of prayer","For the fields are full of harvest, and the barns full of grain","For the sea is full of ships, and the markets full of goods"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 7:23",verse:"Make a chain: for the land is full of bloody crimes, and the city is full of violence.", insight:"The chain is for the criminals; a land full of violence forges its own fetters."},
{q:"When mischief comes upon mischief, what would perish from the priest?", options:["The law","The crown","The sword","The trumpet"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 7:26",verse:"Mischief shall come upon mischief, and rumour shall be upon rumour; then shall they seek a vision of the prophet; but the law shall perish from the priest, and counsel from the ancients.", insight:"In the darkest days, even the guides lose their way; hold the law yourself, do not rent your conscience to priests."},
{q:"What shall the king do?", options:["The king shall mourn","The king shall rejoice","The king shall flee","The king shall dance"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 7:27",verse:"The king shall mourn, and the prince shall be clothed with desolation, and the hands of the people of the land shall be troubled: I will do unto them after their way, and according to their deserts will I judge them; and they shall know that I am the LORD.", insight:"The highest mourn like the lowest; rank cannot exempt a man from the day of the LORD."}
]},
{n:8, name:"Abominations in the Temple", seal:{ref:"Ezekiel 8:18",verse:"Therefore will I also deal in fury: mine eye shall not spare, neither will I have pity: and though they cry in mine ears with a loud voice, yet will I not hear them."}, facts:["Did you know this temple vision is dated to the very day: the sixth year, the sixth month, the fifth day of the month, as the elders of Judah sat before Ezekiel (Ezekiel 8:1)?","Did you know that among the seventy elders secretly burning incense to idols stood Jaazaniah the son of Shaphan, the son of one of good King Josiah's trusted scribes (Ezekiel 8:11)?","Did you know the 'greater abominations' climax with about twenty-five men standing between the porch and the altar with their backs to the temple, worshipping the sun toward the east (Ezekiel 8:16)?"], questions:[
{q:"When did this vision come?", options:["In the sixth year, in the sixth month, in the fifth day of the month","In the first year, in the first month, on the first day","In the thirtieth year, in the fourth month, on the fifth day","In the ninth year, in the tenth month, on the tenth day"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 8:1",verse:"And it came to pass in the sixth year, in the sixth month, in the fifth day of the month, as I sat in mine house, and the elders of Judah sat before me, that the hand of the Lord GOD fell there upon me.", insight:"God dates His visions; what He shows is history, not imagination."},
{q:"From the loins downward, what was the appearance of the glory?", options:["Fire","Water","Smoke","Cloud"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 8:2",verse:"Then I beheld, and lo a likeness as the appearance of fire: from the appearance of his loins even downward, fire; and from his loins even upward, as the appearance of brightness, as the colour of amber.", insight:"The same glory that comforted in the plain now comes to confront; God is fire to the impenitent."},
{q:"From the loins upward, what was the appearance?", options:["As the appearance of brightness, as the colour of amber","As the whiteness of snow","As the blackness of night","As the greenness of the field"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 8:2",verse:"Then I beheld, and lo a likeness as the appearance of fire: from the appearance of his loins even downward, fire; and from his loins even upward, as the appearance of brightness, as the colour of amber.", insight:"Brightness above, fire below; the God of glory is both beautiful and terrible."},
{q:"By what did the hand take hold of Ezekiel?", options:["By a lock of his head","By the hem of his garment","By the staff in his hand","By the shoulder of his robe"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 8:3",verse:"And he put forth the form of an hand, and took me by a lock of mine head; and the spirit lifted me up between the earth and the heaven, and brought me in the visions of God to Jerusalem, to the door of the inner gate that looketh toward the north; where was the seat of the image of jealousy, which provoketh to jealousy.", insight:"God can lift a man by a lock of hair; the Spirit's grip is sure, however strange the hold."},
{q:"What was Ezekiel told to behold when he went in?", options:["The wicked abominations that they do here","The glory of the LORD filling the house","The priests offering the morning sacrifice","The elders praying in the court"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 8:9",verse:"And he said unto me, Go in, and behold the wicked abominations that they do here.", insight:"Go in and behold: God makes the prophet look closely at sin; we cannot repent of what we refuse to see."},
{q:"What sat at the place where he was brought?", options:["The seat of the image of jealousy, which provoketh to jealousy","The ark of the covenant of the LORD","The throne of the king of Judah","The table of shewbread"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 8:3",verse:"And he put forth the form of an hand, and took me by a lock of mine head; and the spirit lifted me up between the earth and the heaven, and brought me in the visions of God to Jerusalem, to the door of the inner gate that looketh toward the north; where was the seat of the image of jealousy, which provoketh to jealousy.", insight:"An idol in God's house: the image of jealousy sits where only God should reign; He will not share His temple."},
{q:"What was there, according to the vision in the plain?", options:["The glory of the God of Israel","The army of the Chaldeans","The council of the elders","The treasure of the temple"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 8:4",verse:"And, behold, the glory of the God of Israel was there, according to the vision that I saw in the plain.", insight:"Glory and abomination stood side by side, but not for long; God's presence will not dwell with idols."},
{q:"Where was the image of jealousy?", options:["Northward at the gate of the altar, in the entry","Southward at the gate of the court, in the corner","Eastward at the porch, by the door","Westward at the wall, behind the temple"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 8:5",verse:"Then said he unto me, Son of man, lift up thine eyes now the way toward the north. So I lifted up mine eyes the way toward the north, and behold northward at the gate of the altar this image of jealousy in the entry.", insight:"The idol stood at the very gate of the altar; corruption had reached the place of sacrifice."},
{q:"What were the abominations doing to God?", options:["Causing Him to go far off from His sanctuary","Drawing Him nearer to His people","Pleasing Him with their zeal","Hiding Him from the nations"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 8:6",verse:"He said furthermore unto me, Son of man, seest thou what they do? even the great abominations that the house of Israel committeth here, that I should go far off from my sanctuary? but turn thee yet again, and thou shalt see greater abominations.", insight:"Sin does not merely offend God; it drives Him from His own house. Guard the sanctuary of your heart."},
{q:"What did Ezekiel see at the door of the court?", options:["A hole in the wall","A golden door","A sleeping guard","A broken altar"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 8:7",verse:"And he brought me to the door of the court; and when I looked, behold a hole in the wall.", insight:"The hole in the wall hints at hidden sins; what men do in secret, God digs up and displays."},
{q:"What appeared when Ezekiel dug in the wall?", options:["A door","A window","A pit","A stairway"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 8:8",verse:"Then said he unto me, Son of man, dig now in the wall: and when I had digged in the wall, behold a door.", insight:"Behind the wall was a door to darkness; dig into secret sin and you will find it has a room."},
{q:"What was pourtrayed upon the wall round about?", options:["Every form of creeping things, and abominable beasts, and all the idols of the house of Israel","The stories of the patriarchs and the kings","The words of the law and the prophets","The names of the tribes of Israel"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 8:10",verse:"So I went in and saw; and behold every form of creeping things, and abominable beasts, and all the idols of the house of Israel, pourtrayed upon the wall round about.", insight:"Their secret gallery was full of creeping things; the walls of the heart display what the heart worships."},
{q:"How many ancients of the house of Israel stood before the idols?", options:["Seventy men","Twelve men","Seven men","Forty men"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 8:11",verse:"And there stood before them seventy men of the ancients of the house of Israel, and in the midst of them stood Jaazaniah the son of Shaphan, with every man his censer in his hand; and a thick cloud of incense went up.", insight:"Seventy leaders, and every one with a censer; when the leaders fall, the incense of idolatry fills the room."},
{q:"Who stood in the midst of the seventy?", options:["Jaazaniah the son of Shaphan","Zedekiah the son of Josiah","Gedaliah the son of Ahikam","Jeremiah the son of Hilkiah"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 8:11",verse:"And there stood before them seventy men of the ancients of the house of Israel, and in the midst of them stood Jaazaniah the son of Shaphan, with every man his censer in his hand; and a thick cloud of incense went up.", insight:"Even the son of a good scribe can go wrong; a godly father does not guarantee a faithful son."},
{q:"What did the ancients say in the dark?", options:["The LORD seeth us not; the LORD hath forsaken the earth","The LORD is with us; the LORD will defend us","The LORD is far off; the LORD will return","The LORD is silent; the LORD will forget"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 8:12",verse:"Then said he unto me, Son of man, hast thou seen what the ancients of the house of Israel do in the dark, every man in the chambers of his imagery? for they say, The LORD seeth us not; the LORD hath forsaken the earth.", insight:"'The LORD seeth us not' is the oldest lie in the dark; there is no darkness to Him."},
{q:"Whom were the women weeping for at the north gate of the LORD's house?", options:["Tammuz","Baal","Ashtoreth","Molech"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 8:14",verse:"Then he brought me to the door of the gate of the LORD’S house which was toward the north; and, behold, there sat women weeping for Tammuz.", insight:"They wept for a dead god at the gate of the living God's house; misplaced tears are the saddest worship."},
{q:"How many men worshipped the sun between the porch and the altar?", options:["About five and twenty men","About twelve men","About seventy men","About three men"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 8:16",verse:"And he brought me into the inner court of the LORD’S house, and, behold, at the door of the temple of the LORD, between the porch and the altar, were about five and twenty men, with their backs toward the temple of the LORD, and their faces toward the east; and they worshipped the sun toward the east.", insight:"Twenty-five men with their backs to the temple; to worship the sun is to turn your back on God."},
{q:"Which way did their faces turn?", options:["Toward the east","Toward the west","Toward the north","Toward the south"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 8:16",verse:"And he brought me into the inner court of the LORD’S house, and, behold, at the door of the temple of the LORD, between the porch and the altar, were about five and twenty men, with their backs toward the temple of the LORD, and their faces toward the east; and they worshipped the sun toward the east.", insight:"Faces east, backs to the temple: the posture tells the story; you cannot face the creature and the Creator at once."},
{q:"What had they filled the land with?", options:["Violence","Wisdom","Wealth","Peace"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 8:17",verse:"Then he said unto me, Hast thou seen this, O son of man? Is it a light thing to the house of Judah that they commit the abominations which they commit here? for they have filled the land with violence, and have returned to provoke me to anger: and, lo, they put the branch to their nose.", insight:"Idolatry and violence walk together; a nation that forgets God soon forgets its neighbor."},
{q:"What did they put to their nose?", options:["The branch","The censer","The veil","The crown"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 8:17",verse:"Then he said unto me, Hast thou seen this, O son of man? Is it a light thing to the house of Judah that they commit the abominations which they commit here? for they have filled the land with violence, and have returned to provoke me to anger: and, lo, they put the branch to their nose.", insight:"They put the branch to their nose, a gesture of contempt; the small signs of scorn reveal a hardened heart."}
]},
{n:9, name:"The Mark and the Slaughter", seal:{ref:"Ezekiel 9:4",verse:"And the LORD said unto him, Go through the midst of the city, through the midst of Jerusalem, and set a mark upon the foreheads of the men that sigh and that cry for all the abominations that be done in the midst thereof."}, facts:["Did you know the mark of mercy went only on the foreheads of those who sighed and cried over the abominations done in Jerusalem (Ezekiel 9:4)?","Did you know judgment was commanded to begin at God's own sanctuary, with the ancient men before the house (Ezekiel 9:6)?","Did you know Ezekiel fell on his face and pleaded, 'wilt thou destroy all the residue of Israel,' even while the slaying went on (Ezekiel 9:8)?"], questions:[
{q:"With what did those in charge of the city come?", options:["Every man with his destroying weapon in his hand","Every man with his trumpet in his hand","Every man with his offering in his hand","Every man with his staff in his hand"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 9:1",verse:"He cried also in mine ears with a loud voice, saying, Cause them that have charge over the city to draw near, even every man with his destroying weapon in his hand.", insight:"The destroyers answer God's call promptly; judgment, too, is obedient to His voice."},
{q:"How did He cry in Ezekiel's ears?", options:["With a loud voice","With a whisper","With a song","With a sigh"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 9:1",verse:"He cried also in mine ears with a loud voice, saying, Cause them that have charge over the city to draw near, even every man with his destroying weapon in his hand.", insight:"God cries aloud when the city will not listen; the louder the call, the nearer the end."},
{q:"Who came from the way of the higher gate toward the north?", options:["Six men, every man with a slaughter weapon in his hand","Three priests, every man with a censer in his hand","Seven elders, every man with a scroll in his hand","Twelve soldiers, every man with a shield in his hand"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 9:2",verse:"And, behold, six men came from the way of the higher gate, which lieth toward the north, and every man a slaughter weapon in his hand; and one man among them was clothed with linen, with a writer’s inkhorn by his side: and they went in, and stood beside the brasen altar.", insight:"Six with slaughter weapons: the number is enough; God's judgments need no multitude."},
{q:"How was the one man among them distinguished?", options:["Clothed with linen, with a writer's inkhorn by his side","Clothed in scarlet, with a sword at his side","Clothed in sackcloth, with ashes on his head","Clothed in purple, with a crown on his head"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 9:2",verse:"And, behold, six men came from the way of the higher gate, which lieth toward the north, and every man a slaughter weapon in his hand; and one man among them was clothed with linen, with a writer’s inkhorn by his side: and they went in, and stood beside the brasen altar.", insight:"Linen for purity, an inkhorn for mercy; even in slaughter, God sends a scribe to mark the mourners first."},
{q:"Where had the glory of the God of Israel gone?", options:["Up from the cherub to the threshold of the house","Down from the mountain to the river of Chebar","Out from the city to the Mount of Olives","Back to the holy of holies"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 9:3",verse:"And the glory of the God of Israel was gone up from the cherub, whereupon he was, to the threshold of the house. And he called to the man clothed with linen, which had the writer’s inkhorn by his side;", insight:"The glory moves to the threshold, ready to leave; when God prepares to depart, the house is already judged."},
{q:"From where had the glory gone up?", options:["From the cherub, whereupon he was","From the ark, whereupon it rested","From the altar, whereupon it stood","From the mercy seat, whereupon it dwelt"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 9:3",verse:"And the glory of the God of Israel was gone up from the cherub, whereupon he was, to the threshold of the house. And he called to the man clothed with linen, which had the writer’s inkhorn by his side;", insight:"The glory lifts from the cherub; when the presence stirs, watch where it goes."},
{q:"Upon whose foreheads was the mark to be set?", options:["Upon the men that sigh and that cry for all the abominations","Upon the priests that offer in the temple","Upon the elders that sit in the gate","Upon the children that play in the streets"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 9:4",verse:"And the LORD said unto him, Go through the midst of the city, through the midst of Jerusalem, and set a mark upon the foreheads of the men that sigh and that cry for all the abominations that be done in the midst thereof.", insight:"The mark is for the mourners, not the mighty; God seals those whose hearts break over sin."},
{q:"Through what was the man in linen to go?", options:["Through the midst of the city, through the midst of Jerusalem","Through the midst of Babylon, through the midst of the nations","Through the midst of the temple, through the midst of the court","Through the midst of the field, through the midst of the valley"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 9:4",verse:"And the LORD said unto him, Go through the midst of the city, through the midst of Jerusalem, and set a mark upon the foreheads of the men that sigh and that cry for all the abominations that be done in the midst thereof.", insight:"Mercy walks the same streets as judgment; the scribe goes through the city before the swords do."},
{q:"What were the others told to do?", options:["Go after him through the city, and smite","Go before him out of the city, and watch","Stand beside him in the temple, and pray","Follow him to the river, and wash"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 9:5",verse:"And to the others he said in mine hearing, Go ye after him through the city, and smite: let not your eye spare, neither have ye pity:", insight:"Judgment follows mercy through the city; the mark first, then the sword."},
{q:"Were their eyes to spare?", options:["Let not your eye spare, neither have ye pity","Let your eye spare the young, and pity the old","Let your eye spare the righteous, and pity the poor","Let your eye spare the city, and pity the temple"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 9:5",verse:"And to the others he said in mine hearing, Go ye after him through the city, and smite: let not your eye spare, neither have ye pity:", insight:"No pity in the execution: when God says the time is come, even mercy steps aside."},
{q:"Whom were they to slay utterly?", options:["Old and young, both maids, and little children, and women","Only the soldiers, and the men of war","Only the priests, and the false prophets","Only the strangers, and the sojourners"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 9:6",verse:"Slay utterly old and young, both maids, and little children, and women: but come not near any man upon whom is the mark; and begin at my sanctuary. Then they began at the ancient men which were before the house.", insight:"Utterly: the judgment spares no age or rank; sin had corrupted the whole city, and the whole city falls."},
{q:"Where was the slaying to begin?", options:["At My sanctuary","At the city gates","At the king's palace","At the marketplace"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 9:6",verse:"Slay utterly old and young, both maids, and little children, and women: but come not near any man upon whom is the mark; and begin at my sanctuary. Then they began at the ancient men which were before the house.", insight:"Judgment begins at the house of God; those nearest the light are judged first."},
{q:"What were they told to do to the house?", options:["Defile the house, and fill the courts with the slain","Cleanse the house, and fill the courts with singers","Guard the house, and fill the courts with guards","Repair the house, and fill the courts with builders"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 9:7",verse:"And he said unto them, Defile the house, and fill the courts with the slain: go ye forth. And they went forth, and slew in the city.", insight:"The defiled temple is filled with the slain; what men polluted with idols, God fills with judgment."},
{q:"Where did they go forth and slay?", options:["In the city","In the temple","In the wilderness","In the field"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 9:7",verse:"And he said unto them, Defile the house, and fill the courts with the slain: go ye forth. And they went forth, and slew in the city.", insight:"From the courts to the city streets; judgment that starts in the sanctuary does not stop there."},
{q:"What did Ezekiel do while they were slaying?", options:["He fell upon his face, and cried","He fled from the city","He shut his eyes, and slept","He lifted his hands, and sang"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 9:8",verse:"And it came to pass, while they were slaying them, and I was left, that I fell upon my face, and cried, and said, Ah Lord GOD! wilt thou destroy all the residue of Israel in thy pouring out of thy fury upon Jerusalem?", insight:"The prophet falls on his face while God strikes; intercession is the right posture in the day of wrath."},
{q:"What did Ezekiel ask?", options:["Wilt thou destroy all the residue of Israel in thy pouring out of thy fury upon Jerusalem?","Wilt thou spare the temple from the fire?","Wilt thou save the children from the sword?","Wilt thou remember thy covenant forever?"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 9:8",verse:"And it came to pass, while they were slaying them, and I was left, that I fell upon my face, and cried, and said, Ah Lord GOD! wilt thou destroy all the residue of Israel in thy pouring out of thy fury upon Jerusalem?", insight:"Ezekiel pleads for the residue; the true prophet loves the people even while he prophesies their doom."},
{q:"How great was the iniquity of Israel and Judah?", options:["Exceeding great","Small and hidden","Old and forgotten","Light and passing"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 9:9",verse:"Then said he unto me, The iniquity of the house of Israel and Judah is exceeding great, and the land is full of blood, and the city full of perverseness: for they say, The LORD hath forsaken the earth, and the LORD seeth not.", insight:"Exceeding great: God names the sin plainly because the sin was plain; honesty about sin is the start of mercy."},
{q:"With what was the land full, and the city full?", options:["The land full of blood, and the city full of perverseness","The land full of grain, and the city full of merchants","The land full of flocks, and the city full of singers","The land full of silver, and the city full of builders"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 9:9",verse:"Then said he unto me, The iniquity of the house of Israel and Judah is exceeding great, and the land is full of blood, and the city full of perverseness: for they say, The LORD hath forsaken the earth, and the LORD seeth not.", insight:"Blood in the land, perverseness in the city; the iniquity was not private, it filled everything."},
{q:"What would God do with their way?", options:["Recompense their way upon their head","Forget their way forever","Cover their way with mercy","Turn their way to good"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 9:10",verse:"And as for me also, mine eye shall not spare, neither will I have pity, but I will recompense their way upon their head.", insight:"Their way returns upon their head; the measure men give is the measure they receive."},
{q:"What did the man clothed with linen report?", options:["I have done as thou hast commanded me","I have spared whom thou badest me spare","I have marked more than thou commandedst","I have finished before the evening"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 9:11",verse:"And, behold, the man clothed with linen, which had the inkhorn by his side, reported the matter, saying, I have done as thou hast commanded me.", insight:"'I have done as Thou hast commanded me': the servant's whole report is obedience; let that be ours."}
]},
{n:10, name:"The Glory Departs", seal:{ref:"Ezekiel 10:18",verse:"Then the glory of the LORD departed from off the threshold of the house, and stood over the cherubims."}, facts:["Did you know the cherubims' wheels were full of eyes round about, even the wheels themselves (Ezekiel 10:12)?","Did you know Ezekiel heard a voice cry out to the wheels, simply, 'O wheel' (Ezekiel 10:13)?","Did you know this chapter records the moment the glory of the LORD departed from the threshold of the temple and stood over the cherubims (Ezekiel 10:18)?"], questions:[
{q:"What appeared above the head of the cherubims?", options:["As it were a sapphire stone, as the appearance of the likeness of a throne","As it were a golden crown, as the appearance of a king","As it were a brazen altar, as the appearance of fire","As it were a silver trumpet, as the appearance of war"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 10:1",verse:"Then I looked, and, behold, in the firmament that was above the head of the cherubims there appeared over them as it were a sapphire stone, as the appearance of the likeness of a throne.", insight:"Above the cherubims, a throne of sapphire; even in judgment, God reigns from glory."},
{q:"What was the man in linen to scatter over the city?", options:["Coals of fire from between the cherubims","Ashes of repentance from the altar","Seeds of wheat from the field","Drops of water from the river"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 10:2",verse:"And he spake unto the man clothed with linen, and said, Go in between the wheels, even under the cherub, and fill thine hand with coals of fire from between the cherubims, and scatter them over the city. And he went in in my sight.", insight:"Coals of fire over the city: the same fire that purifies the altar consumes the impenitent."},
{q:"On which side of the house did the cherubims stand?", options:["On the right side","On the left side","On the north side","On the east side"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 10:3",verse:"Now the cherubims stood on the right side of the house, when the man went in; and the cloud filled the inner court.", insight:"The right side: the place of readiness; the cherubims stand prepared for what God commands."},
{q:"What filled the house?", options:["The cloud","The smoke","The fire","The wind"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 10:4",verse:"Then the glory of the LORD went up from the cherub, and stood over the threshold of the house; and the house was filled with the cloud, and the court was full of the brightness of the LORD’S glory.", insight:"The cloud fills the house as the glory lifts; God's presence both fills and withdraws."},
{q:"What was the sound of the cherubims' wings like?", options:["As the voice of the Almighty God when He speaketh","As the rushing of a mighty river","As the roaring of a lion in the forest","As the thunder of a distant storm"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 10:5",verse:"And the sound of the cherubims’ wings was heard even to the outer court, as the voice of the Almighty God when he speaketh.", insight:"Their wings sound like God's own voice; heaven's servants move with heaven's authority."},
{q:"Where did the man clothed with linen stand?", options:["Beside the wheels","Beside the altar","Beside the threshold","Beside the cherubims"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 10:6",verse:"And it came to pass, that when he had commanded the man clothed with linen, saying, Take fire from between the wheels, from between the cherubims; then he went in, and stood beside the wheels.", insight:"Beside the wheels, ready for the coals; obedience takes its place before the command is finished."},
{q:"Who put the fire into the hands of the man in linen?", options:["One cherub","One seraph","One elder","One priest"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 10:7",verse:"And one cherub stretched forth his hand from between the cherubims unto the fire that was between the cherubims, and took thereof, and put it into the hands of him that was clothed with linen: who took it, and went out.", insight:"A cherub hands the fire to the man; heaven's ministers serve the mission of judgment."},
{q:"What appeared under the wings of the cherubims?", options:["The form of a man's hand","The shape of a lion's paw","The likeness of an eagle's talon","The print of an ox's hoof"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 10:8",verse:"And there appeared in the cherubims the form of a man’s hand under their wings.", insight:"A man's hand under the wings: the mighty cherubims work with a human touch; God's power is never inhuman."},
{q:"What was the colour of the wheels?", options:["As the colour of a beryl stone","As the colour of a sapphire stone","As the colour of burning brass","As the colour of pure gold"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 10:9",verse:"And when I looked, behold the four wheels by the cherubims, one wheel by one cherub, and another wheel by another cherub: and the appearance of the wheels was as the colour of a beryl stone.", insight:"Beryl, a sea-green stone; the wheels gleam like the deep, full of mystery and motion."},
{q:"What was the likeness of the four wheels?", options:["As if a wheel had been in the midst of a wheel","As if a star had been in the midst of a star","As if a crown had been in the midst of a crown","As if a gate had been in the midst of a gate"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 10:10",verse:"And as for their appearances, they four had one likeness, as if a wheel had been in the midst of a wheel.", insight:"A wheel within a wheel: God's purposes turn in every direction at once; He never needs to turn around."},
{q:"When they went, how did they turn?", options:["They turned not as they went","They turned to the right","They turned to the left","They turned back again"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 10:11",verse:"When they went, they went upon their four sides; they turned not as they went, but to the place whither the head looked they followed it; they turned not as they went.", insight:"They turned not: God's chariot never changes course; His counsel stands forever."},
{q:"What were their bodies, wings, and wheels full of?", options:["Eyes round about","Feathers of gold","Flames of fire","Jewels of light"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 10:12",verse:"And their whole body, and their backs, and their hands, and their wings, and the wheels, were full of eyes round about, even the wheels that they four had.", insight:"Full of eyes: nothing escapes the wheels of God; His providence sees every road."},
{q:"What was cried unto the wheels in Ezekiel's hearing?", options:["O wheel","O fire","O wind","O glory"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 10:13",verse:"As for the wheels, it was cried unto them in my hearing, O wheel.", insight:"O wheel: heaven itself addresses the instruments of judgment; even wheels have their calling."},
{q:"Name the four faces of every cherub.", options:["The face of a cherub, the face of a man, the face of a lion, the face of an eagle","The face of a man, the face of an ox, the face of a lion, the face of an eagle","The face of a seraph, the face of a man, the face of a lamb, the face of a dove","The face of an angel, the face of a child, the face of a horse, the face of a bear"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 10:14",verse:"And every one had four faces: the first face was the face of a cherub, and the second face was the face of a man, and the third the face of a lion, and the fourth the face of an eagle.", insight:"Cherub, man, lion, eagle: wisdom, humanity, strength, and swiftness; heaven's servants bear every excellence."},
{q:"Where had Ezekiel seen this living creature before?", options:["By the river of Chebar","By the river of Jordan","By the sea of Galilee","By the brook of Kidron"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 10:15",verse:"And the cherubims were lifted up. This is the living creature that I saw by the river of Chebar.", insight:"The same vision returns; God confirms His word by repeating it. What you saw at Chebar, you see at Jerusalem."},
{q:"When the cherubims went, what did the wheels do?", options:["The wheels went by them","The wheels stood still","The wheels rolled backward","The wheels sank to the earth"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 10:16",verse:"And when the cherubims went, the wheels went by them: and when the cherubims lifted up their wings to mount up from the earth, the same wheels also turned not from beside them.", insight:"The wheels go with the cherubims; God's instruments never lag behind His Spirit."},
{q:"Why did the wheels move and stand with the cherubims?", options:["For the spirit of the living creature was in them","For the wind of heaven drove them","For the hands of angels pushed them","For the fire within burned them"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 10:17",verse:"When they stood, these stood; and when they were lifted up, these lifted up themselves also: for the spirit of the living creature was in them.", insight:"One spirit in wheels and wings; when God's Spirit is in the work, every part moves as one."},
{q:"Where did the glory of the LORD go?", options:["It departed from off the threshold of the house, and stood over the cherubims","It returned to the holy of holies","It descended into the inner court","It ascended into the firmament"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 10:18",verse:"Then the glory of the LORD departed from off the threshold of the house, and stood over the cherubims.", insight:"The glory departs from the threshold; the saddest verse in Ezekiel is God leaving His own house."},
{q:"At which gate did the cherubims stand?", options:["At the door of the east gate of the LORD's house","At the door of the north gate of the city","At the door of the west gate of the temple","At the door of the south gate of the court"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 10:19",verse:"And the cherubims lifted up their wings, and mounted up from the earth in my sight: when they went out, the wheels also were beside them, and every one stood at the door of the east gate of the LORD’S house; and the glory of the God of Israel was over them above.", insight:"The east gate: the glory pauses at the exit; even in leaving, God moves slowly, giving time to repent."},
{q:"What did Ezekiel now know?", options:["That they were the cherubims","That they were the seraphims","That they were the angels of the nations","That they were the spirits of the prophets"], a:0, ref:"Ezekiel 10:20",verse:"This is the living creature that I saw under the God of Israel by the river of Chebar; and I knew that they were the cherubims.", insight:"'I knew that they were the cherubims': the vision of chapter one finds its name; God lets us grow into understanding."}
]}
]);
